> "saiaspa" would not be accepted by the PEG morphology, but not because
> of any 5-letter rule, but because it would break as "sa iaspa". (The
> PEG morphology does not require a pause before i/u as semivowels), I
> changed the example to "sa'aispa".

Yes I need to get camxes and jbofi'e so I can test things out. I
wonder how much of the decision of where camxes breaks things is
driven by the grammar ? does jaiaspa act different than saiaspa ,
caiaspa , daiaspa, faiaspa, etc etc. Also seems that what experimental
cmavo the parser does or doesn't know could effect results in a few
circumstances.

>
> That page was done before the Lojban morphology existed, I should
